    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002af', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002ae', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P2, category capacity, 4 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 3 runbook match(es), 6 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 4 service(s) over 94 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 24 evidence items; 7 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 2 direct, 2 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-03 03:33:00.000000', '2026-11-03 05:07:00.000000', '2026-11-03 01:59:00.000000', '2026-11-03 03:33:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P2", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Claims Processing (JP) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "capacity", "candidate_service_names": ["claims-document-renderer", "claims-apim"], "incident_summary": "Claims Processing (JP): intermittent 502 errors and pod restarts. Users and systems of Claims Processing (JP) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["intermittent 502 errors and pod restarts"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P2", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P2"}', N'Parts of Claims Processing (JP) intermittently fail because a service keeps running out of memory and restarting. Users see occasional errors when documents are rendered. A temporary memory increase and restart stabilise it; the underlying memory leak needs a code fix.', N'Claims Processing (JP) saw intermittent 502 errors while pods of claims-document-renderer restarted repeatedly. Kubernetes reports containers OOMKilled and backing off, and restart counts increased.', N'Containers of claims-document-renderer reach their 1 GiB memory limit and are killed by the kernel [E4]. Memory grows by roughly 300 MB per hour, which indicates a leak in the document renderer rather than a one-off spike. While pods restart the gateway has no healthy backend and returns 502.', N'Relieve memory pressure with a temporary limit increase and restart; fix the renderer''s unreleased image buffers.

1. Confirm which pods are close to the limit (read-only).

```
kubectl top pods -n claims-docs
```

2. Temporarily raise the memory limit of claims-document-renderer to 2Gi.

```
kubectl set resources deployment/claims-document-renderer -n claims-docs --limits=memory=2Gi
```

3. Restart the deployment to clear leaked memory.

```
kubectl rollout restart deployment/claims-document-renderer -n claims-docs
```

4. Durable fix: release image buffers after each render and add a memory-based alert at 80 percent of the limit.

**Verify:** kubectl get pods -n claims-docs shows no new OOMKilled restarts for 30 minutes. Gateway 502 rate returns to baseline.

**Rollback:** kubectl rollout undo deployment/claims-document-renderer -n claims-docs  # if the restart makes things worse', N'["Which release introduced the memory growth?", "Can the renderer be load tested with a memory profile before the next release?"]', 0.82, N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002cc', N'{"nodes": [{"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "serviceName": "claims-document-renderer", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "serviceName": "claims-apim", "serviceType": "api_management", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "direct"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "serviceName": "claims-api", "serviceType": "aks", "criticalityTier": "tier_1", "impactLevel": "indirect"}, {"serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c", "serviceName": "claims-intake-func", "serviceType": "function_app", "criticalityTier": "tier_2", "impactLevel": "indirect"}], "edges": [{"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "kind": "calls"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009", "kind": "calls"}, {"fromServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c", "toServiceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006", "kind": "calls"}], "impactedSlos": [{"sloId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000233", "sliId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000230", "applicationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "applicationName": "Claims Processing (JP)", "serviceId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "serviceName": "claims-apim", "sliName": "claims-apim: Gateway availability", "sliKind": "availability", "isHeadline": true, "isApproximate": false, "targetPercentage": 99.5, "rollingWindowDays": 30, "compliancePercentage": 99.923, "errorBudgetRemainingPercentage": 84.5, "errorBudgetRemainingMinutes": 182.5, "errorBu