    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002ff', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000062', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000002fe', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P3, category dependency, 1 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 1 runbook match(es), 0 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 1 service(s) over 139 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 2 evidence items; 0 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Few strong signals found; asking the planner for up to three extra read-only queries"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 1 direct, 0 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-11 05:25:00.000000', '2026-11-11 07:44:00.000000', '2026-11-11 03:06:00.000000', '2026-11-11 05:25:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P3", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "dependency", "candidate_service_names": ["benefits-portal"], "incident_summary": "Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS): benefits portal slow and intermittently unavailable. Users and systems of Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["benefits portal slow and intermittently unavailable"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P3", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P3"}', N'The benefits portal is slow or unavailable because our vendor is having a service problem in the Asia-Pacific region. We are tracking the vendor''s incident and will update employees when it is resolved.', N'Employees cannot reliably open the benefits portal of Employee Benefits Portal (SaaS); Keigan''s synthetic probe fails about 40 percent of the time with HTTP 503.', N'The SaaS vendor is experiencing degraded performance in its APAC region, which its status page confirms, and our probes see HTTP 503 and multi-second latency. No MetLife change is involved.', N'Nothing can be fixed on the Keigan side; track the vendor incident, inform employees and agree an ETA.

1. Subscribe to the vendor status page incident and share the link with the incident channel.
2. Post a banner or intranet notice that enrolment may be slow or unavailable.
3. Open a priority ticket with the vendor support channel quoting the synthetic probe failure times.

**Verify:** Synthetic probes succeed for three consecutive runs.

