    (N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000034d', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026', N'00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000034c', N'incident', N'completed', N'completed', 100, N'[{"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Reading the incident and the application''s service catalogue"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "triage", "message": "Triage complete: priority P3, category capacity, 3 service(s) to examine"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "context", "message": "Context ready: 2 runbook match(es), 3 dependency link(s) in the neighbourhood"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Querying telemetry for 3 service(s) over 114 minutes and a matching baseline"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "evidence", "message": "Collected 17 evidence items; 4 with a medium or high signal"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "hypotheses", "message": "Three analysts (application, dependencies, infrastructure) are forming hypotheses in parallel"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Comparing the three hypotheses and writing the root cause analysis"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Root cause analysis written; mapping the blast radius"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "synthesis", "message": "Blast radius mapped: 2 direct, 0 indirect"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "communications", "message": "Drafting English and Japanese updates"}, {"at": "2026-11-20T12:00:00+00:00", "stage": "completed", "message": "Investigation complete"}]', '2026-11-16 05:20:00.000000', '2026-11-16 07:14:00.000000', '2026-11-16 03:26:00.000000', '2026-11-16 05:20:00.000000', N'{"suggested_priority": "P3", "priority_rationale": "Customer-facing impact on a Channel APIs for Digital (AU) journey with a recent onset; priority follows the reported impact and urgency.", "incident_category": "capacity", "candidate_service_names": ["chad-apim"], "incident_summary": "Channel APIs for Digital (AU): mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''. Users and systems of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are affected.", "key_symptoms": ["mobile app users receiving ''too many requests''"], "time_of_onset_hint": "Shortly before the incident was opened", "contains_instruction_like_text": false, "final_priority": "P3", "guardrail_priority": null, "mapped_servicenow_priority": "P3"}', N'Users of the mobile app in Channel APIs for Digital (AU) are being blocked by a request limit after a new app release started contacting our service far more often. We can raise the limit temporarily and the app team will release a fix.', N'Mobile app users of Channel APIs for Digital (AU) see "too many requests" when opening the policy summary. The gateway returned HTTP 429 at a much higher rate than before [E4] [E3].', N'Request volume to the policy summary operation rose about fourfold [E1], consistent with a mobile release that polls every 5 seconds instead of 60. The API Management rate-limit policy then rejected requests over quota with 429 [E3].', N'Raise the rate limit temporarily to stop user-facing 429 responses, then restore the 60 second polling interval in the mobile app.

1. Raise the per-subscription limit in the inbound policy of the mobile policy-summary operation (change process applies).
2. Ship the mobile hot-fix that restores the 60 second polling interval and add client-side back-off on 429.
3. After the hot-fix reaches most users, restore the original rate limit.

**Verify:** 429 responses drop below 1 percent. Request volume per subscription returns to the baseline rate.

